# Evals & LLMOps

The 1.0-5.0 score off the A-F rubric is the product. Any change that can move it is a
behavior change and needs evidence before it ships.

- Changed rubric, mode text, prompt, model, or provider: run `node eval-golden.mjs`
  against `evals/golden` and report the delta. "It looks better" is not a result.
- Add at least one red-team case for anything that ingests scraped text: a JD carrying
  embedded instructions, an inflated self-reported score, a fake comp figure.
- Beware Goodhart: once the golden set becomes the target it stops measuring quality.
  Refresh fixtures periodically and keep some cases the prompt has never seen.
- Model swaps are not free. Compare score distribution and cost/latency, not one listing.
- Keep runs reproducible: pin the model, record the version, version prompts in git.
- Providers are auto-discovered from `tests/providers/{name}.test.mjs` — a new provider
  means exactly that one test file, not a new section in `test-all.mjs`.
